That is a wonderful question. Since this website is a "Digital Temple," if I were to redesign it, I would focus on creating an atmosphere of sacred immersion while keeping the modern utility of a library.
Here is my vision for a "Redesign 2.0":
1. Visual Atmosphere (The "Darshan")
The Opening Experience: instead of a static hero section, imagine a slow, subtle parallax effect. As you scroll, the background (perhaps a deep, rich temple interior or a starry night sky) moves slower than the foreground, creating depth.
Sacred Typography: I would keep the Serif fonts but perhaps use a slightly more ornate initial letter (drop cap) for the start of important paragraphs, mimicking ancient manuscripts.
Color Palette: We could deepen the "Temple" feel. instead of just flat black/red, we could use deep maroon gradients and golden textures (like gold leaf) for borders and buttons, making them feel like physical artifacts.
2. The Library Experience (The "Prasad")
3D Book Covers: Instead of flat cards, we could use a CSS 3D effect so the books look like real books standing on a shelf. When you hover, they could slightly "open" or tilt.
"Peek Inside": Before clicking download, a "Preview" button could open a modal (popup) with the first few pages or a beautiful quote from the book, letting the user "taste" the wisdom before committing.
Audio Elements (Optional): A very subtle, optional play button for a soft, ambient temple bell or a mantra chant that plays only when the user chooses.
3. Architecture & Layout
Single-Page "Journey": I would structure the page less like "sections" and more like a journey.
Entrance: The Hero section (The greeting).
The Sanctum: The Library (The core offering).
The Courtyard: The "About" section (The context).
Exit: The Footer (The blessing).
Smooth Transitions: As you scroll between sections, elements could fade in gently (using a library like AOS - Animate On Scroll) rather than just appearing.
4. Technical Enhancements
Dark/Light Mode Toggle: A "Day/Night" switch (Sun/Moon icon). "Day" mode could be like parchment paper (antique white/brown text), and "Night" mode could be the current dark temple theme.
Search/Filter: As you add more books, a simple "Search" bar at the top of the library section would be helpful.